opum-doc ruling B on ADR 0024, 2026-10-30T17:12:49Z, verbatim: "B. Keep max_tokens at 36000, and the ADR states the RULE while referring to the LIST.
Reason: the 13 names have one source of truth, the canonical constant in profile.ts. A second copy in the ADR will drift the next time a name is added, and this is a security list where drift matters. Ruling timestamps are tracker facts, not architecture. Raising a budget to fit a duplicate is the wrong precedent.
The ADR MUST still be self-contained on the design. State:
(a) the invariant: a declared header may not make the request differ from what the approval prompt showed (method, path, authority, framing);
(b) the refused categories by name: credentials, routing/authority, framing, hop-by-hop, and method/path/authority overrides, with two or three examples each;
(c) the matching rule: case-fold, then "_" to "-", before every reserved or refused lookup, in both positions including auth.name;
(d) the error contract: the detail is Ward's canonical constant only, never profile bytes;
(e) the snapshot-version policy;
(f) a pointer to the constant by path and symbol, plus the decision ids DEC-248 and WCLI-98, where the rulings are recorded verbatim. No timestamps.
If lore check still fails with that text, send me the measured token count before raising anything." SUPERSEDED the same hour by the 17:15:29Z ruling below on the budget, after the measured count (about 36064 for the minimal draft) was reported.
